  "id": "COMPOUND:25003 - PROTEIN:5537",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and KNS-62, with multiple pathways converging on the target KNS-62 through different intermediates. The first pathway links 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid directly to A704, which is then targeted by palmarumycin CP18, ultimately leading to KNS-62. The second and third pathways show that 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid also targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4C and NCI-H46, which in turn target the same compound that leads to KNS-62. These findings suggest that 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid may act as a common modulator of KNS-62 through distinct downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where the compound influences KNS-62 via multiple molecular routes, possibly through enzyme inhibition or other regulatory interactions. The evidence supports a role for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid in modulating KNS-62, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
